course: dictionary
lesson: 2288
title: The Cretaceous: a period and a chalky word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A capital letter can change a word's meaning. The Cretaceous, with a big C, is a name for a period of Earth's history. «Earth's history is divided into eons, eras and periods, such as the Jurassic, about 200 to 145 million years ago, and the Cretaceous.» Read the words around it: a period is a stretch of time, so the Cretaceous is a time, not a place.
explain: The Cretaceous was the last period of the age of dinosaurs. It lasted from about 145 to 66 million years ago. Tyrannosaurus rex and Triceratops lived then, and the period ended when a huge asteroid hit the Earth and most dinosaurs died out.
explain: With a small c, cretaceous is an adjective that means made of chalk, or like chalk. Ask what the sentence is describing. If it is talking about white cliffs or rock, the chalk meaning fits. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check.
fact: The Cretaceous is a period in Earth's history, from about 145 to 66 million years ago.
fact: It was the last period of the age of dinosaurs, and it ended when a huge asteroid hit the Earth.
fact: The name comes from the Latin word «creta», which means chalk.
fact: Chalk rocks, such as the White Cliffs of Dover, formed during this period.
fact: With a small c, «cretaceous» means made of chalk or like chalk.
exercise: «Earth's history is divided into eons, eras and periods, such as the Jurassic, and the Cretaceous.» In this sentence, what is the Cretaceous? | A type of cloud | *A period of Earth's history | A kind of sweet made from sugar | A tiny fish that lives in rivers
exercise: What ended the Cretaceous period, according to science lessons? | A very cold winter in one town | *A huge asteroid hitting the Earth | A rainstorm that lasted for years | A school trip to the museum
exercise: A rock is described as «cretaceous», with a small c. What might it be made of? | *Chalk | Iron | Water | Wood
test: Which dinosaurs lived in the Cretaceous? | *Tyrannosaurus rex and Triceratops | Sabre-toothed cats | Dodos | Woolly mammoths
test: The Latin word «creta» means what, and why is the period named after it? | Water, because the sea was everywhere | *Chalk, because chalk rocks like the White Cliffs of Dover formed then | Dinosaur, because dinosaurs lived then | Asteroid, because one hit the Earth
exam: «The cliffs were white and cretaceous, like the cliffs of Dover.» In this sentence, what does cretaceous mean? | Full of water | Very hot | Made of iron | *Made of chalk, or like chalk
